#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
mactop: zero-root system & GPU monitor for macOS (Apple Silicon & Intel).

The macOS sibling of ptop (PowerShell Top) and shtop (Shell Top): same layout,
themes and controls. A single file, Python 3 standard library only, no root/sudo
required. Reads Mach kernel statistics, libproc, sysctl, IOKit/IORegistry,
IOHID thermal sensors, AppleSMC (when readable), and libIOReport directly via
ctypes and ioreg.

Controls:
  [Q] / [Esc] : Quit (Esc clears an active filter first; Ctrl+C also quits)
  [/]         : Filter processes by name or PID (Enter keeps, Esc clears)
  [Up]/[Down] : Select process (also PgUp/PgDn/Home/End; the list scrolls)
  [K] / [Del] : Kill selected process (asks: [Y] SIGTERM, [9] SIGKILL)
  [P]         : Toggle Per-Core CPU bars view
  [T]         : Cycle color themes (Midnight, Cyberpunk, Matrix, Gruvbox, Nord)
  [C]         : Sort processes by CPU%
  [M]         : Sort processes by Memory
  [G]         : Prioritize GPU processes
  [I]         : Sort processes by disk I/O rate
  [+] / [-]   : Increase / Decrease refresh speed
"""

